rsetup-next (0.5.0-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Release the native CLI, TUI, and Web SBC control center.
  * Add bounded, read-only APT mirror latency and index speed tests.
  * Display system and Radxa measurements separately with bilingual results.
  * Add curl and CA certificates for verified HTTPS mirror sampling.
  * Support native EFI/BLS overlays shared by Dragon Q6A and Q8B.
  * Include Q8B pin functions and corrected live hardware probing.
  * Run all browser regression tests during Debian package builds.
  * Ship the rsetup-controller configuration example as documentation under
    /usr/share/doc/rsetup-controller instead of installing
    /etc/default/rsetup-controller; the unit's ConditionPathExists keeps the
    service inactive until the operator creates that file at mode 0600.
    Installing and upgrading never start, restart or stop the service.
  * Pin the build tool floor debhelper (>= 13.11.6~), the first release whose
    dh_installsystemd resolves units under /usr/lib/systemd/system.

 -- xzl <xiangzelong@radxa.com>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 18:18:14 +0800

rsetup-next (0.5.0~alpha1-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Initial package for the Rust control center.
  * Replace the legacy Bash package split with one CLI, TUI, and Web binary.
  * Build Cargo dependencies offline from a package-local cache.
  * Link the executable statically for Debian 12 runtime compatibility.
  * Add a Polkit-authorized fixed-operation helper for unprivileged GUIs.
  * Migrate SSH, Docker, and reversible sleep management operations.
  * Add overlay, read-only GPIO, camera snapshot, and thermal policy tools.
  * Add native LED and backed-up SPI boot flash management.
  * Add a validated temperature-driven pwm-fan curve service.

 -- xzl <xiangzelong@radxa.com>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0800
